{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubjectSubscription","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make one with the subject’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"makeSubscription()"},{"type":"text","text":". It subscribes when it is made, exactly like the subject’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterator: a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CurrentValueSubject"},{"type":"text","text":"’s subscription starts with the current value, and every value sent after that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is buffered for it, without limit, until "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The difference is cancellation. Cancelling a task waiting in an iterator’s "},{"code":"next()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ends that iterator’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subscription and discards its buffer. Cancelling a task waiting in a subscription’s "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" throws"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from that call only: the subscription stays subscribed, and a later "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" returns the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values sent before and after the cancellation, in order. That suits a consumer that runs in rounds, such as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch run that is cancelled and started again, and must not miss what was sent between rounds."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The subscription unsubscribes when its last copy is released. It conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncIteratorProtocol","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"operator can read it through ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncIteratorSequence","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"; a cancelled read then ends that operator’s run with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and leaves the subscription for the next run.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Example","anchor":"Example","type":"heading"},{"code":["let events = PassthroughSubject<String>()","let subscription = events.makeSubscription()","","let firstRound = Task { try await subscription.next() }","firstRound.cancel() \/\/ Throws CancellationError from that wait; nothing is lost.","_ = await firstRound.result","","events.send(\"launch\")","events.send(\"login\")","let first = try await subscription.next()  \/\/ \"launch\"","let second = try await subscription.next() \/\/ \"login\""],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"style":"important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Wait on a subscription from one task at a time. Calling ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" while another call on the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subscription is still waiting traps.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Important","type":"aside"}]}],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"fileName":"SubjectSubscription.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Afluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription.swift#L40"},"symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SubjectSubscription"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubjectSubscription","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"SubjectSubscription","modules":[{"name":"Afluent"}],"externalID":"s:7Afluent19SubjectSubscriptionV"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/AsyncIteratorProtocol-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations"}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/subjectsubscription"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A place in a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/CurrentValueSubject"},{"type":"text","text":" that a consumer can stop waiting on and come back"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to, keeping every value sent in between."}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent"]]},"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Afluent\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Afluent\/ScI"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"references":{"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/SubjectSubscription":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubjectSubscription","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SubjectSubscription","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/subjectsubscription","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A place in a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/CurrentValueSubject"},{"type":"text","text":" that a consumer can stop waiting on and come back"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to, keeping every value sent in between."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SubjectSubscription","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Afluent/ScI":{"title":"_Concurrency.AsyncIteratorProtocol","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/ScI"},"doc://Afluent/s16SendableMetatypeP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/s16SendableMetatypeP","title":"Swift.SendableMetatype","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/PassthroughSubject":{"title":"PassthroughSubject","abstract":[{"text":"A subject that broadcasts values to multiple consumers without storing a current value.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Unlike ","type":"text"},{"code":"CurrentValueSubject","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"PassthroughSubject","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does not retain the most recent value.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This is an ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that allows multiple tasks to asynchronously consume values and mimics Combine’s PassthroughSubject.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/passthroughsubject","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PassthroughSubject","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PassthroughSubject","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent":{"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/afluent","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent","title":"Afluent"},"doc://Afluent/s8SendableP":{"title":"Swift.Sendable","type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/s8SendableP"},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/AsyncIteratorSequence":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncIteratorSequence","url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/asynciteratorsequence","type":"topic","abstract":[],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AsyncIteratorSequence"}],"role":"symbol","title":"AsyncIteratorSequence","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AsyncIteratorSequence"}]},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/SubjectSubscription/next()":{"title":"next()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/next()","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/subjectsubscription\/next()","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"next","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Waits for the next value sent to the subject.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/CurrentValueSubject":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A subject that broadcasts its current value and all subsequent values to multiple consumers."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It can also handle completion events, including normal termination and failure with an error."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncSequence"},{"type":"text","text":" that allows multiple tasks to asynchronously consume values and mimics Combine’s CurrentValueSubject."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CurrentValueSubject"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CurrentValueSubject"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/CurrentValueSubject","type":"topic","title":"CurrentValueSubject","url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/currentvaluesubject"},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/SubjectSubscription/AsyncIteratorProtocol-Implementations":{"title":"AsyncIteratorProtocol Implementations","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/subjectsubscription\/asynciteratorprotocol-implementations","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SubjectSubscription\/AsyncIteratorProtocol-Implementations"}}}